From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tompta1 <546706+tompta1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:00:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: apple-h9p: Add the T8011

The A10X (T8011) has six root ports, a different common status register
(0x24), a pipe-clock gate in LINKSTS bit 2 and its own PHY, root complex
and port tunables (AppleT8011PCIe, iPadOS 17.7.11 21H461; the iPad Pro 10.5
and 12.9 (2017) device trees carry the same values). Port 0 is the ANS
storage port, which runs in NVMe mode and trains for 8 GT/s; other ports
train at the device tree's max-link-speed.

The port count becomes match data (four for every existing SoC), and a root
port can take the MSI range its firmware assigns ("apple,msi-vector-range",
eight vectors at eight times the port number when absent, as before). The
sleep, recovery and late-port loops use the SoC's port count.

A port whose link does not come up is reported and left down, as on the
T8010, instead of failing the whole controller: storage and Wi-Fi do not
take each other down, and "apple,link-retry-after-power-cycle" works here
too.

No change on the other SoCs: their port count stays four and their MSI
programming is the same value as before.

[Orchard: from OrchardLinux/orchard#205 (tompta1, 09038adf),
 kernel/patches/drivers/pci/0042 and 0043 squashed. Matched on
 "apple,t8011-pcie" instead of "apple,j120-pcie"; the J120 profile validator
 (fixed DART addresses, apertures, MSI ranges and link speeds) dropped,
 keeping only the wait for each port's DART; any root port set up from the
 device tree instead of ports 0 and 2 only; the Wi-Fi and storage tunable
 tables merged (they were the same apart from one storage entry); a port
 failure no longer fails the probe; the pwrctrl "reg_on_only" mode and
 port compatible dropped: the Wi-Fi node uses the existing BCM4355 power
 sequence.]

Assisted-by: LLM
